WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.888
Life isn't too short.

2
00:00:01.888 --> 00:00:04.581
We spend too much of it carelessly.

3
00:00:05.831 --> 00:00:07.754
Seneca rejects the common complaint

4
00:00:07.754 --> 00:00:09.677
that life is cruelly brief.

5
00:00:09.677 --> 00:00:12.369
We're given enough time to do important

6
00:00:12.369 --> 00:00:14.677
things, if we arrange it well.

7
00:00:15.927 --> 00:00:17.850
The real problem is leakage:

8
00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:21.312
hours drained by distraction, indulgence, and drifting without purpose.

9
00:00:22.927 --> 00:00:26.004
We do not have a very short time,

10
00:00:26.004 --> 00:00:29.081
but we lose a great deal of it.

11
00:00:29.081 --> 00:00:32.542
Life is long enough for the most important things.

12
00:00:33.792 --> 00:00:36.100
The point stings because it puts

13
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.408
the issue back in our hands.

14
00:00:38.408 --> 00:00:40.715
A year can feel like nothing

15
00:00:40.715 --> 00:00:42.638
when it's spent on autopilot.

16
00:00:43.888 --> 00:00:46.581
Or it can feel rich, when it's

17
00:00:46.581 --> 00:00:49.273
aimed at a few things that matter.

18
00:00:50.523 --> 00:00:52.062
Look at yesterday honestly.

19
00:00:52.062 --> 00:00:55.138
Estimate how many hours went to things you'd

20
00:00:55.138 --> 00:00:58.215
choose again, and how many simply leaked away.
